From: macos-local research
Subject: [PATCH] 32K 2-way CPUJumpCache and L1.5 end-to-end PAuth op cache with PAC->AUT pre-population

Restore 256 page buckets (16,384 2-way sets = 32,768 entries) in CPUJumpCache,
remove the net-negative 256 KiB pauth_qarma_l2 table, and add a 64 KiB
L1.5-resident 2-way end-to-end PAuth instruction cache (active only when
x-pauth-memo=on on AArch64 without EL2/EL3/M; cleared on reset and post-load)
with algebraic PAC->AUT inverse pre-population on canonical pointers and a
12,288-iteration startup equivalence selftest.

